# Jaecoo 7 five-door SUV, 2024 onwards.
#
# The Jaecoo 7: the larger SUV with the vertical-slat grille, the slim
# headlamps and the full-width tail bar. UK orders opened 27 November 2024
# and sales began in January 2025. The later facelift is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaecoo_7
#
# Dimensions 4.451-4.501 x 1.865 x 1.670 m, wheelbase 2.650 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a manufacturer studio cut-out, perpendicular
# and level with all wheels visible; the other images show a UK showroom car
# and the rear. The studio rear is used because no clean UK rear photograph
# exists.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the JAECOO UK palette: Granite White, Basalt Black,
# Pearl Silver and Amazonite Blue. Weights 15, 13, 12, 10, total 50,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 90/315, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 90. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 2025 intro, retires staggered 2045-2048.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaecoo-7.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaecoo-7.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaecoo-7/ (gitignored; manufacturer press images held
# as internal reference only).
#
# Accepted deviations: 4.475 m is the body length chosen within the published
# 4.451-4.501 m range, and the axle spacing is corrected to 2.650 m. The lamp
# internals, the badging and the D-pillar detail are simplified.


obj=citycar
name=Jaecoo7(GraniteWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=15
intro_year=2025
intro_month=1
retire_year=2048
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=315

